---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { t, type Lang } from '../../lib/i18n';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [{ params: { lang: 'zh' } }, { params: { lang: 'en' } }];
}

const lang = Astro.params.lang as Lang;
const otherLang: Lang = lang === 'zh' ? 'en' : 'zh';

const APP_URL = 'https://repeatclip.mengyahu.com';
const REPO_URL = 'https://github.com/mengyahuUSTC-PU/repeatclip';
---

<Base
  title={t(lang, 'projects.title')}
  description={
    lang === 'zh'
      ? '我为自己的真实需求做的小工具，第一个是 RepeatClip：循环播放 YouTube 视频的任意片段。'
      : 'Small tools I build for real problems in my own life. First up: RepeatClip, a YouTube section looper.'
  }
  lang={lang}
  path={`/${lang}/projects/`}
  altPath={`/${otherLang}/projects/`}
>
  <h1>{t(lang, 'projects.title')}</h1>

  <div class="project-intro">
    {lang === 'zh' ? (
      <p>
        我为自己的真实需求做的小工具。做出来能用就行，也顺手分享给需要的人。
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        Small tools I build for real problems in my own life. They only need to work for me,
        but if they are useful to someone else, they are here.
      </p>
    )}
  </div>

  <ul class="post-list">
    <li class="post-card wide">
      <p class="post-meta">{lang === 'zh' ? '2026 · 已上线' : '2026 · Live'}</p>
      <h3><a href={APP_URL}>RepeatClip</a></h3>
      {lang === 'zh' ? (
        <p>循环播放 YouTube 视频的任意片段，调慢速度，反复练习。</p>
      ) : (
        <p>Loop any part of a YouTube video and practice it at your own speed.</p>
      )}

      <div class="project-story">
        {lang === 'zh' ? (
          <>
            <p>我平时跳舞。学一段编舞的时候，我想把其中一小段单独抠出来反复放，先放慢，练顺了再一点点加快。市面上应该有做这件事的产品，但我懒得去找、去比、去装。</p>
            <p>于是我把需求跟 coding agent 讲了一遍，三分钟后就有了一个我自己喜欢的版本：粘贴链接、填好起止时间、选速度，剩下的它自己循环。它有独立网址，链接里带着片段的起止时间，我可以直接发给一起跳舞的姐妹们，她们打开就是我练的那十秒。</p>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <p>
              I dance. When I am learning choreography I want one short section on repeat, slowed down
              first, then a little faster once it starts to stick. There are probably products that do
              this. I did not feel like hunting for one, comparing them, installing anything.
            </p>
            <p>
              So I described what I wanted to a coding agent and had a version I actually liked about
              three minutes later: paste a link, type the start and end times, pick a speed, and it loops. It has
              its own address, and the share link carries the start and end times, so I can send my
              dance friends the exact ten seconds I have been drilling.
            </p>
          </>
        )}
      </div>

      <p class="project-links">
        <a class="project-cta" href={APP_URL}>{lang === 'zh' ? '打开 RepeatClip →' : 'Open RepeatClip →'}</a>
        <a href={REPO_URL}>{lang === 'zh' ? '在 GitHub 查看源码' : 'View source on GitHub'}</a>
      </p>

      <div class="tags">
        {(lang === 'zh'
          ? ['视频练习', 'YouTube', '中英双语']
          : ['Video practice', 'YouTube', 'Bilingual']
        ).map((tag) => <span class="tag">{tag}</span>)}
      </div>
    </li>
  </ul>
</Base>

<style>
  .project-intro { max-width: 40rem; margin: -0.4rem 0 1.6rem; }
  .project-intro p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.8; margin: 0; }
  .project-story { max-width: 40rem; }
  .project-story p { margin-top: 0.9rem; }
  .project-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.2rem; align-items: baseline; margin-top: 1.1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .project-cta { font-weight: 700; }
</style>
